# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# A row is as tall as the letters in it, and the letters are a preference.
#
# The height was worked out once, when the shell started, and handed to
# everything that draws a list -- so changing the face redrew the words at
# their new size into rows still sized for the old one.  At 16 px they did
# not fit; the fix is that the height is taken again every frame.
#
# Asked here the only way a script can see it: how many rows the window
# SHOWS.  A taller row means fewer of them in the same window, which is
# arithmetic no redraw can fake.
wait 15
expect-visible-rows 10
note and the Deskbar's own leaf, which is a row of the strip like any other
expect-pixel 990 36 d8d8d8
note put the interface up to 16 px from the window that chooses it
click 980 20
wait 4
menu-pick Settings
wait 4
menu-pick Fonts
wait 12
expect-title Fonts
expect-font Sans 12
click 652 300
wait 12
expect-font Sans 14
click 652 310
wait 12
expect-font Sans 16
note and back to the folder, whose rows are now taller than they were
key w ctrl
wait 8
expect-visible-rows 8
note the leaf reaches four pixels further down than it did: the strip is
note drawn in the face it is now being asked to hold
expect-pixel 990 36 ffcb00
note and Get Info, whose height was written down as 300 for a 12 px face:
note at this one its foot reaches forty pixels further, which is the eight
note rows of the permissions page plus the two tab strips growing
click-row 1
key i ctrl
wait 10
expect-title a.txt info
expect-pixel 300 392 d8d8d8
note and it follows the face back DOWN without being reopened: the window
note is never closed here, so what moves its foot is the refit, not the
note size it happened to be given when it opened
click 980 20
wait 4
menu-pick Settings
wait 4
menu-pick Fonts
wait 12
expect-title Fonts
click 382 435
wait 12
expect-font Sans 12
expect-pixel 300 392 336698
